data: {"type":"data-vendo-build-failed","data":{"toolCallId":"hcall_4_909bbd2f-c02a-4098-86b2-c6c1584e76fd","reason":"app build failed: This app wasn't created, because it didn't pass the checks that keep an app honest: The binding `sum(spending.data.amount)` sums the `amount` field from the spending insights (322,200 cents = $3,222.00), but the `format=\"money\"` attribute almost certainly divides by 100 for display — however the real problem is that `spending.data` is a category-level summary array, not a transaction list, and the amounts are already in cents; the sum is correct in value but must be verified that the money formatter divides by 100 (i.e. displays $3,222.00, not $322,200.00) — if the formatter does NOT divide by 100, the displayed total will be wrong by a factor of 100; confirm the `format=\"money\"` helper divides cents by 100 before shipping. The cashflow `average(cashflow.data.out)` averages the `out` values across all months including the partial/zero-income August row (out: 322200) and a zero-in month, producing a distorted monthly average; dividing that by 4.33 gives a weekly figure that is not a reliable typical weekly spend — the comparison note will show a misleading difference; use only complete months (e.g. May–July) to compute the average, or use a dedicated typical-spend field if available. The `difference()` call operates on raw cent integers but the result is rendered inline in a sentence with no currency formatting or divide-by-100, so the displayed text will read something like \"Spending is tracking 123456 versus your usual weekly average\" — the difference value must be divided by 100 and formatted as $X,XXX.XX before interpolation. The `amount` column uses `format=\"money\"` on values from `spending.data` which are already in integer cents (e.g. 285000); if the formatter divides by 100 this is correct ($2,850.00), but if it does not, it will display raw cents — verify the formatter divides by 100, and if not, divide explicitly before binding."}}

